# caramel-vault: how the Caramel Fabric mod works and the traps each part hides; _map.md lists
# the topics. Read by the /gold skill and its vault_lint.py.
#
# dates = forbidden. The owner's ruling: a note says how Caramel works for anyone building it,
# so it has no date. A claim bound to a version names the version (Minecraft 26.3, Loom 1.18.4);
# git keeps the when. The owner's quoted words stay in docs/DESIGN.md, where they are the reason
# for a choice.
#
# No status_lives_in: the vault holds no status. _map.md, "What lives outside the vault", names
# where it lives: all outside the vault.
#
# The vault lives inside the repository and goes into the same commits as the code it
# describes. .obsidian/ is gitignored.
#
# Checkers (gold step 0), run from the repository root:
#   ./gradlew build                         must pass, game tests included ("All N required tests
#                                           passed"); rebuild before trusting a jar in build/libs/
#   ./gradlew runDatagen && git status --porcelain src/main/generated
#                                           only the changes you expect
#   unzip -l build/libs/caramel-*[0-9].jar  the mod jar (not -sources) lists LICENSE_caramel
#                                           and LICENSE-ASSETS_caramel
# Beyond those, verification is reading build.gradle, gradle.properties, fabric.mod.json, the
# mixin configs and .github/, and reproducing a trap in a scratch copy of the project before
# writing its error message down.
dates = forbidden
